      "writtenOn": "2022-06-06T21:02:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e OK. Will the EC send out (VIRTUAL_MUX) host events to the AP when DP alt mode is entered?\n\nI thought when we discussed the feature progression diagrams we decided to skip the virtual mux step for external mux boards? \n\n\u003e I haven\u0027t thought about this TBH. How would it work for Intel-style situations, where the retimer is programmed by the EC, but the mux by the AP (there, orientation has been an issue in the past)?  It\u0027s probably fine to auto-fill for external mux+retimer situations, but the mixed use case is the one to look out for.\n\nAt the moment, the EC would fill in the polarity it has on the PD connection for the external retimer and the AP would set whatever it wanted on the internal one.  It does seem wise to expect the AP to set polarity though, if we\u0027re going to hit issues with tricky mux chains. I\u0027ll put in a CL to change that behavior\n\n\u003e Feature flag. This makes the code paths a lot cleaner in the driver (and makes it easy for userspace to determine whether a board supports a certain feature or not).\n\nI\u0027ll work on a CL for that one",
      "parentUuid": "e24c4f73_172761df",
      "revId": "48f6e378bec40a4550490367cc6ed9eb1aea9cc5",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
