      "message": "\u003e Yep, that\u0027s right; the AP alt mode driver will direct the entry, so no events required. At present though, the EC  DP module is governing alt mode entry (IIUC); so in the current state, how does the EC tell the AP that DP alt mode has been entered and we need to update the muxes/retimers (my apologies if I inadvertently conflated VIRTUAL_MUX usage here, but that\u0027s the closest analog I am familiar with)?\n\nContext: On the AP, the Mux driver will be linked to the main port driver. So the kernel\u0027s port driver would be the one telling the mux driver that port X is in Y state. `ectool` doesn\u0027t exercise the same codde paths as the mux driver would.",
      "parentUuid": "677382aa_8287c7d8",
